IMPORT prelude

-- Community Care Endowment Fund Act 2005 (Singapore) -- who the ComCare Fund's income may help and how it may be paid out
-- (ss 6, 11), gifts and capital (ss 3(3), 5(3)-(5), 8), the financial year (s 9), who may audit (s 12(1), (2)), the offences
-- (ss 13, 15), liability of officers and partners (s 16), composition (s 17), and removal of Council members (Schedule para 1(3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CCEFA2005.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; no later
-- amendment is annotated in the text. The SSO metadata beside it reads "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0164 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has yet
-- asked a sharper question. SCOPED to what a person seeking help, a donor, a social service organisation or someone questioned by
-- the auditor actually meets. Not encoded: the establishment and administration provisions as such (ss 3(1), (2), 4, 7), the
-- Minister's accounting and reporting duties (ss 10, 14), the auditor's powers and report contents (s 12(3)-(6)), regulation-making
-- (s 18), and the Council's meeting procedure (Schedule paras 2-5). No regulations made under s 17 or s 18 were retrieved, so
-- whether any offence is compoundable, and how anyone applies for help, is unknown here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Community Care Endowment Fund Act 2005 -- the ComCare Fund`

DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    `a citizen`
    `a permanent resident`
    `a family member of a citizen or permanent resident`
    `a foreigner with no such family tie`

DECLARE Need IS ONE OF
    `income to meet basic needs`
    `a child's developmental issues`
    `help to integrate into society`
    `none of the listed needs`

§§ `6(1) -- who the income of the Fund may help`

-- s 6(1): the income may be applied to "(a) the provision of assistance to citizens and permanent residents of Singapore and their
-- family members living in Singapore with financial or other difficulties to enable them to attain sufficient income to meet their
-- basic needs"; (b) "the developmental issues faced by children from families of citizens and permanent residents of Singapore
-- living in Singapore with financial or other difficulties"; (c) the same people "who require help to integrate into society";
-- (d) programmes to enhance the capacity of the community to do (a) to (c).
--
-- READING (an inference, not stated): "living in Singapore" is read as qualifying the family members in (a) and (c) -- the nearest
-- antecedent -- so a citizen or PR living abroad is not excluded by the words. In (b) it is read as qualifying the family. Another
-- reader could apply it to everyone. "Family member" is not defined in s 2.
GIVEN `the status` IS A Status, `living in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `in financial or other difficulties` IS A BOOLEAN, `the need` IS A Need
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is within the objects of the Fund` IF
        `in financial or other difficulties`
    AND CONSIDER `the need`
        WHEN `none of the listed needs` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a child's developmental issues` THEN
            `living in Singapore`
            AND CONSIDER `the status`
                WHEN `a foreigner with no such family tie` THEN FALSE
                OTHERWISE TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the status`
            WHEN `a citizen` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a permanent resident` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a family member of a citizen or permanent resident` THEN `living in Singapore`
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6(2), 5(4) and 11 -- how money may be paid out`

-- s 6(2): the Minister "may" authorise the income to be paid out for "(a) the provision of grants to be given to individuals or
-- families through organisations; (b) the provision of grants to be given to organisations to carry out programmes consistent with
-- the objects of the Fund; (c) such other purposes consistent with the objects of the Fund, as may be prescribed".
-- s 5(4): "The capital moneys of the ComCare Fund must not be used for any purpose other than for investment."
-- s 11: "A payment must not be made out of the ComCare Fund unless the payment is approved by the Minister or any authorised officer."
--
-- Nothing in the Act gives an individual a right to a grant: the Minister "may" authorise, and grants to individuals go "through
-- organisations". A grant paid straight to an individual fits only if it is a prescribed purpose under (c).
DECLARE Payout IS ONE OF
    `a grant to an individual or family through an organisation`
    `a grant paid directly to an individual`
    `a grant to an organisation for a programme consistent with the objects`
    `a grant to an organisation for a programme outside the objects`

GIVEN `the payout` IS A Payout, `paid from capital` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved by the Minister or an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prescribed as a purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment may be made` IF
        (NOT `paid from capital`)
    AND `approved by the Minister or an authorised officer`
    AND CONSIDER `the payout`
        WHEN `a grant to an individual or family through an organisation` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a grant to an organisation for a programme consistent with the objects` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a grant paid directly to an individual` THEN `prescribed as a purpose`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5(3) -- gifts and bequests`

-- s 5(3): "Despite the terms of any gift or bequest, all gifts and bequests given or made for the purposes of the ComCare Fund must
-- be paid into the Fund as capital moneys." With s 5(4), a gift may only be invested; only its income is spent.
GIVEN `given for the purposes of the Fund` IS A BOOLEAN, `the donor directs that it be spent at once` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gift becomes capital that may only be invested` IF
    `given for the purposes of the Fund`

§§ `3(3), 5(5) and 8 -- what income is left to pay out`

-- s 3(3): net income from investments is the income received "adding to, or deducting from" it any profit derived or loss sustained
-- on realisation. s 5(5): where there is "a permanent diminution of the capital moneys", the Minister "must, before paying out any
-- income of the Fund, make good such diminution from the income". s 8: "All expenses incurred in connection with the administration
-- of the ComCare Fund, including the cost of auditing the accounts of the Fund, must be defrayed out of the income of the Fund."
-- The Act does not order the make-good against the expenses; both are taken off income here and the result is floored at nil
-- (an inference: the Act does not say what happens when income falls short).
GIVEN `investment income received` IS A NUMBER, `realisation profit` IS A NUMBER, `realisation loss` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net income` MEANS
    `investment income received` PLUS `realisation profit` MINUS `realisation loss`

GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below nil` MEANS
    IF `amount` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `amount`

GIVEN `the year's net income` IS A NUMBER, `permanent diminution not yet made good` IS A NUMBER, `administration expenses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income available for grants` MEANS
    `not below nil` (`the year's net income` MINUS `permanent diminution not yet made good` MINUS `administration expenses`)

§§ `9 -- the financial year`

-- s 9: "The financial year of the ComCare Fund begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
-- Given a calendar month (1-12) and year, the year in which that financial year began.
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year began in` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` MINUS 1

§§ `12(1), (2) -- who may audit the Fund`

-- s 12(1): audited "by the Auditor-General or such other auditor as may be appointed annually by the Minister in consultation with
-- the Auditor-General". (2): "A person is not qualified for appointment as an auditor under subsection (1) unless he or she is a
-- public accountant who is registered or deemed to be registered under the Accountants Act 2004."
-- READING (an inference): (2) is read as applying to the "other auditor" appointed by the Minister, not to the Auditor-General, who
-- is not "appointed" under (1).
GIVEN `is the Auditor-General` IS A BOOLEAN, `appointed by the Minister this year` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Auditor-General was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN, `a registered public accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may audit the Fund` IF
        `is the Auditor-General`
    OR  (`appointed by the Minister this year` AND `the Auditor-General was consulted` AND `a registered public accountant`)

§§ `13 -- failing to give the auditor information`

-- s 13(1): the auditor "may require any person to furnish him or her with such information in the possession of that person or to
-- which that person has access". (2): a person who "without reasonable excuse, fails to comply ... or who otherwise hinders,
-- obstructs or delays the auditor" is guilty of an offence, "a fine not exceeding $1,000". No imprisonment; the Act does not put
-- the burden of the excuse on the accused.
GIVEN `required by the auditor to give information` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `hindered, obstructed or delayed the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the auditor offence` IF
        (`required by the auditor to give information` AND (NOT `complied`) AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`))
    OR  `hindered, obstructed or delayed the auditor`

§§ `15 -- false statements and documents`

-- s 15: any person who, "for any purpose connected with this Act", (a) "knowingly makes any false statement to the Minister or an
-- authorised officer or to the auditor or a person authorised by him or her"; or (b) produces or furnishes "any document which he
-- or she knows to be false in a material particular" to the same people -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000".
-- The listed recipients do not include the organisations through which grants reach individuals (s 6(2)(a)). Whether a false
-- statement to such an organisation is "to ... an authorised officer" depends on facts the Act does not give; it is not one here.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `the Minister`
    `an authorised officer`
    `the auditor`
    `a person authorised by the auditor`
    `a social service organisation giving out a grant`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a listed recipient` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `a social service organisation giving out a grant` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `for a purpose connected with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `made a false statement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew the statement was false` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave a document false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew the document was false` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the false information offence` IF
        `for a purpose connected with the Act`
    AND `is a listed recipient` `the recipient`
    AND (    (`made a false statement` AND `knew the statement was false`)
         OR  (`gave a document false in a material particular` AND `knew the document was false`))

§§ `13, 15 -- maximum penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to assist the auditor`
    `giving false information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to assist the auditor` THEN 1000
    WHEN `giving false information` THEN 5000

§§ `16 -- officers, partners and members`

-- s 16(1): where an offence by a body corporate is proved "(a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of an officer;
-- or (b) to be attributable to any neglect on his or her part", the officer is guilty too; (3) the same for a partner of a
-- partnership; (4) for an officer or governing-body member of an unincorporated association. (5): "body corporate" includes a
-- limited liability partnership; "officer" includes "any person purporting to act in any such capacity".
GIVEN `the organisation committed an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the offence is attributable to the individual's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer or partner is also guilty` IF
        `the organisation committed an offence under the Act`
    AND (`consented or connived` OR `the offence is attributable to the individual's neglect`)

§§ `17 -- composition`

-- s 17(1): the Minister or an authorised officer "may compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a compoundable
-- offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding $500". (2): on payment "no further proceedings may be taken". (3) the offences are
-- prescribed by regulations -- none were retrieved.
GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable` AND `the sum` AT MOST 500

§§ `Schedule para 1(3) -- removing a Council member`

-- Schedule para 1(3): if the Minister is satisfied that a member "(a) is guilty of neglect of duty or misconduct; (b) has become
-- bankrupt or made an arrangement with his or her creditors; (c) is incapacitated by physical or mental illness; or (d) is otherwise
-- unable or unfit to discharge the functions of a member, the Minister may remove him or her from office." (2): a member may resign
-- at any time by written notice to the Minister.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `neglect of duty or misconduct`
    `bankruptcy or an arrangement with creditors`
    `incapacity through physical or mental illness`
    `otherwise unable or unfit`
    `disagreeing with the Minister`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `the Minister is satisfied of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may remove the member` IF
        `the Minister is satisfied of it`
    AND CONSIDER `the ground`
        WHEN `disagreeing with the Minister` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
